    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25495" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπεραι-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>take across, ferry over,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sull.</u>
				27
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be carried over, cross,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθεῦτεν διαπεραιωθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὸν ποταμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.124
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ πάντες διεπεπεραίωντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.23
				</span></i>
			: in aor.
			
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ax.</u>
				370b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολεῶν διεπεραιώθη ξίφη</span> swords
				<i>were unshcathed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				730
			</span></i>.</div>
